    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 the project's surefire config runs the acceptance suite).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a single new, self-contained aspect to satisfy the audit-create rule.\n\n**New file:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerAuditCreationAdvice.java`\n\nIt's an `@Aspect`/`@Component` with one small `@Around` advice on `ClinicService.saveOwner`:\n- captures `owner.isNew()` **before** the save (so it only fires for creates, not updates),\n- lets the save proceed (by which point the id is generated and the sibling `@Before` advices have assigned `customerCode` and `registrationDate`),\n- then emits one line on the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:** I touched exactly one file and added zero changes to any existing function. The only changed \"function\" lives in a brand-new class with no sibling methods, so `WMC_other` is minimal (\u21921) and the method itself is trivial (CC 2). This mirrors the codebase's established pattern of one small aspect per owner-creation rule (`OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice`, `OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice`, etc.) rather than growing the controller or service.\n\nVerified log output during the run:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-01\n```",
